# Normalise line endings in the repository, not in each contributor's checkout.
# Without this, Windows clones get CRLF and Linux clones get LF, so the same
# commit produces different bytes depending on who checked it out -- which shows
# up as spurious whole-file diffs and breaks byte-level comparisons of the data.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Compressed data is binary; never let git touch it.
*.gz binary
*.parquet binary

# Keep the shell/CLI entry points executable where the platform supports it.
*.py text
*.yaml text
*.yml text
*.md text
